## Issue Formats

### Encyclopedia Root (Encyclopedia Index type)

Single root issue linking to all domains:

```markdown
# Encyclopedia Root

Master index of all research domains in Gitopedia.

## Domains

- [Science](https://github.com/gitopedia/gitopedia/issues/127)
- [Arts](https://github.com/gitopedia/gitopedia/issues/XXX)
```

**Issue Type:** Encyclopedia Index

### Domain Issue (Research Domain type)

Top-level domain with back-link to root:

```markdown
# Science

Top-level domain for scientific research.

**Parent:** [Encyclopedia Root](https://github.com/gitopedia/gitopedia/issues/126)

## Categories

- [Science > Physics](https://github.com/gitopedia/gitopedia/issues/124)
- [Science > Geography](https://github.com/gitopedia/gitopedia/issues/125)
```

**Issue Type:** Research Domain

### Category Issue (Research Category type)

Category with back-link to domain:

**Title:** `Science > Physics`

```markdown
# Science > Physics

Physics research topics under the Science domain.

**Domain:** [Science](https://github.com/gitopedia/gitopedia/issues/127)

## Topics

- [Science > Physics > Quantum Mechanics](https://github.com/gitopedia/gitopedia/issues/121)
- [Science > Physics > Thermodynamics](https://github.com/gitopedia/gitopedia/issues/122)
```

**Issue Type:** Research Category

### Topic Issue (Research Topic type)

Topic with back-link to category and article checkboxes:

**Title:** `Science > Physics > Quantum Mechanics`

```markdown
# Quantum Mechanics

Articles about quantum mechanics to research.

**Category:** [Science > Physics](https://github.com/gitopedia/gitopedia/issues/124)

## Articles

- [ ] Quantum Mechanics
- [ ] Schrödinger's Cat
- [x] Wave Function (completed)
- [ ] Heisenberg Uncertainty Principle
```

**Issue Type:** Research Topic

## Bidirectional Linking

Every issue links both up (to parent) and down (to children):

| Level | Links Up To | Links Down To |
|-------|-------------|---------------|
| Root | - | Domains |
| Domain | Root | Categories |
| Category | Domain | Topics |
| Topic | Category | Articles (checkboxes) |

## Topic Selection Flow

When the researcher runs:

1. **Fetch Topics** - Uses GraphQL to get all open issues with "Research Topic" issue type
2. **Filter Available** - Excludes topics that are assigned, have `pending review` label, or have open PRs
3. **Random Selection** - Picks one available topic randomly
4. **Claim Topic** - Assigns itself to the issue to prevent race conditions
5. **Create Branch** - Creates a research branch for all work

## Article Processing Flow

Once a topic is claimed, the researcher iterates:

1. **Parse Articles** - Extracts checkboxes from the issue body
2. **Prioritize Incomplete** - Focuses on unchecked articles first
3. **Create or Improve** - Creates new articles, or improves existing ones
4. **Update Checkbox** - Marks articles as done after creation
5. **Post Summary** - Comments on the issue with all changes
6. **Release Topic** - Unassigns itself when done

## Code Implementation

### Fetching Topic Issues (GraphQL)

```go
// In github/client.go - GetTopicIssues()
query := `query {
  repository(owner: $owner, name: $repo) {
    issues(first: 100, states: OPEN, filterBy: {issueType: "Research Topic"}) {
      nodes { number title body }
    }
  }
}`
```

### Parsing Articles

```go
// In github/client.go
articles := github.ParseArticlesFromBody(issue.GetBody())
// Returns []ResearchArticle{{Name: "Quantum Mechanics", Completed: false}, ...}
```

### Checking Off Articles

```go
// After successful research
newBody := github.CheckArticleInBody(issue.GetBody(), articleName)
gh.UpdateIssueBody(issueNumber, newBody)
```

## Best Practices

1. **Use Full Paths in Titles** - Topic titles include `Domain > Category > Topic`
2. **Always Add Back-Links** - Every issue links to its parent
3. **Update Parent Links** - When creating children, update parent's list
4. **Keep Topics Focused** - 5-20 articles per topic issue
5. **Use Descriptive Names** - Article names become article titles
6. **Set Issue Types via GraphQL** - After creating issues, apply the appropriate issue type

